# /etc/logrotate.d/agent-app  --  B4-1 monitor.log rotation
# Official requirement: max 10 MB per log, max 10 files kept.
# Choice (conservative, valid for BOTH readings of "10 MB"): rotate at 9 MiB = 9437184 bytes (logrotate "9M").
#   - logrotate checks the size only when it runs (daily), so a file can grow past the threshold in between:
#     measured growth is 1 official record (63-73 B) per minute = 90-105 KB/day.
#   - Largest expected rotated file: 9437184 B + ~105 KB = ~9.54 MB, below BOTH 10 MB (10000000 B) and 10 MiB.
#   - A plain "size 10M" (10485760 B) would exceed a decimal 10 MB even without any overshoot.
# This is NOT a hard cap: if logrotate did not run for many days the file could grow further (see Note below).
# Rotate when the active log is 9 MiB or MORE (logrotate 3.21 compares with >=); keep the active
# file + at most 9 rotated files (monitor.log, monitor.log.1 ... monitor.log.9 = 10 files max).
#
# Why rename+create (default) and NOT copytruncate:
#   monitor.sh opens monitor.log only for its single official-record append at the end of a run
#   (open, one short write, close; no descriptor is held while it runs). After a rename the next run simply
#   opens/creates the new active file; a record is never split across files.
#   copytruncate copies then truncates, which can lose lines written between the two steps and
#   splits a running instance's output across two files.
#
# 'su agent-admin agent-core': the log directory is root:agent-core 2770, i.e. group-writable by
#   a non-root group, so logrotate refuses to rotate there unless told which user/group to use.
#   Rotation then runs as agent-admin (member of agent-core, can rename/create in the directory).
#
# Note: the size is only checked when logrotate runs (systemd logrotate.timer = daily, AccuracySec=1h), so this
#   is "rotate once the threshold is reached", NOT a strict maximum-size guarantee. Total on disk: at most
#   10 files (active + .1 ... .9), uncompressed (nocompress), i.e. ~96 MB. First rotation of an empty log: ~100 days.
/var/log/agent-app/monitor.log {
    su agent-admin agent-core
    size 9M
    rotate 9
    create 0660 agent-admin agent-core
    missingok
    notifempty
    nocompress
}
